{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1197159-perhaps-a-really-basic-question","id":1197159,"title":"Perhaps a really basic question?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-19T06:11:41-07:00","id":1197159,"title":"Perhaps a really basic question?","content":"Hey there,<br /> <br /> I've been getting contradicting answers from those who play with me about this question, so I decided to ask it here.<br /> <br /> The book often says a &quot;Gaian&quot; spirit may teach a certain gift. When referring to Gaian spirits, do they mean any Wyld and Weaver spirits? Just Wyld spirits? Ancestor spirits too?<br /> What do they mean by Gaian spirit and what is and what isn't a Gaian spirit?<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance,<br /> TataCavalier<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T06:48:56-07:00","id":1197167,"title":"","content":"Without going into great detail, I definitely suggest checking out the book W20 Umbra: The Velvet Shadow if you are looking for more detail on the subject, I would say that Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm spirts are spirits of that Trait, not Gaia. They are spirits that in concept exist only outside the material realm. Gaian spirits are spirits that are reflections of things that exist, or existed, only because Gaia exists. So typically this would include Animal, Plant, Elemental, Ancestor, and any Incarna spirits as well as their Brood who have sworn allegiance to Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T06:54:30-07:00","id":1197169,"title":"","content":"There are spirits that, rather than being aspected to the Triat, have the aspect of Gaia herself in balance. Ancestor spirits are Gaian spirits, as are some spirits of animals and of the natural elements, and some spirit servants associated with the tribal totems. The line between a spirit of the Wyld and a spirit of Gaia might be a little fuzzy, but Weaver spirits definitely are off the mark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T07:30:34-07:00","id":1197181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1197159-perhaps-a-really-basic-question?p=1197169#post1197169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are spirits that, rather than being aspected to the Triat, have the aspect of Gaia herself in balance. Ancestor spirits are Gaian spirits, as are some spirits of animals and of the natural elements, and some spirit servants associated with the tribal totems. The line between a spirit of the Wyld and a spirit of Gaia might be a little fuzzy, but Weaver spirits definitely are off the mark.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Um cockroach? Easy Credit? Hell there are wyrmy Gaian spirits.. really its a matter of who they serve &quot;first&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T08:50:10-07:00","id":1197218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1197159-perhaps-a-really-basic-question?p=1197169#post1197169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without going into great detail, I definitely suggest checking out the book W20 Umbra: The Velvet Shadow if you are looking for more detail on the subject, I would say that Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm spirts are spirits of that Trait, not Gaia. They are spirits that in concept exist only outside the material realm. Gaian spirits are spirits that are reflections of things that exist, or existed, only because Gaia exists. So typically this would include Animal, Plant, Elemental, Ancestor, and any Incarna spirits as well as their Brood who have sworn allegiance to Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very well written response. I believe I understand now, thank you very much!<br /> I'll make sure to get ahold of that book and read it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1197159-perhaps-a-really-basic-question?p=1197169#post1197169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are spirits that, rather than being aspected to the Triat, have the aspect of Gaia herself in balance. Ancestor spirits are Gaian spirits, as are some spirits of animals and of the natural elements, and some spirit servants associated with the tribal totems. The line between a spirit of the Wyld and a spirit of Gaia might be a little fuzzy, but Weaver spirits definitely are off the mark.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say Weaver spirits are off the mark, which I thought too at first. But then after a few minutes of thought, I remembered that the more progressive and &quot;modern&quot; tribes make pacts with Weaver spirits like the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers, and so I thought they may be added as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}